        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px">The <a href="lfs">Linux From Scratch</a> (LFS) project has announced the release of Linux From Scratch 13.1, a document which will assist people in building their own distribution from source code. This version of LFS includes Linux kernel 7.1.8, glibc 2.44 and GCC 16.2.0. "<span class="Quote">The Linux From Scratch community announces the release of LFS Version 13.1. Major changes include toolchain updates to Binutils 2.47, GCC 16.2.0 and glibc 2.44. In total, 46 packages were updated or added since the last release. Changes to the text have also been made throughout the book. The Linux kernel has also been updated to version 7.1.8. Packages that have security updates include attr, acl, expat, glibc, Linux kernel, Python, systemd, util-linux, vim and zlib. See the Security Advisories page for details. Overall there have been over 200 commits to LFS since the previous stable version of the book.</span>" Visit the project's <a href="https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/news.html">news page</a> to read the brief release announcement. The Linux From Scratch and Beyond Linux From Scratch books can be found on the project's <a href="https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/lfs/download.html">download page</a>: LFS (<a href="table.php?distribution=lfs&amp;pkglist=true&amp;version=13.1#pkglist">pkglist</a>): <a href="https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/lfs/view/13.1-systemd/">13.1 - HTML</a>, <a href="https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/lfs/downloads/13.1-systemd/LFS-SYSD-BOOK-13.1.pdf">13.1 -PDF</a>. Please note that the Beyond Linux From Scratch (BLFS) book has not been updated to version 13.1, so <a href="https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable-systemd/">version 13.0</a> remains the latest BLFS book.</td>
