        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px">The <a href="endeavour">EndeavourOS</a> project has a new release, which is acting as a filler between two major releases. EndeavourOS 2026.08.15 "Titan Nova" fixes some keyboard setup issues, improves support for NVIDIA GPUs, and removes the Budgie desktop environment as an install-time option. "<span class="Quote">Titan Nova's live environment and offline installer are shipping with Calamares 26.03.2.3, Firefox 153.0.4, Linux kernel 7.1.8, Mesa 26.1.7, X.Org Server 21.1.24, nvidia-utils 610.57.04, nvidia-open 610.54.01. Keyboard setup fix - fixed an issue where recent keyboard configuration updates caused setup errors. A temporary patch is in place to ensure everything configures smoothly, with a permanent fix planned in the upcoming Triton release. Improved the experience on the ISO when using the Nouveau drivers for NVIDIA GPUs. Budgie desktop removed - the option to install the Budgie desktop environment has been temporarily removed. The current upstream software version is in a transition phase to newer display technology (Wayland) and isn't providing a default experience we are comfortable with. We expect Budgie to return in future releases.</span>" Additional information is provided in the <a href="https://endeavouros.com/news/titan-nova-is-available/">release announcement</a>. <a href="https://endeavouros.com">Download</a>: <a href="https://mirrors.c0urier.net/linux/endeavouros/iso/EndeavourOS_Titan-Nova-2026.08.15.iso">EndeavourOS_Titan-Nova-2026.08.15.iso</a> (3,718MB, <a href="https://mirrors.c0urier.net/linux/endeavouros/iso/EndeavourOS_Titan-Nova-2026.08.15.iso.sha512sum">SHA512</a>, <a href="https://mirrors.c0urier.net/linux/endeavouros/iso/EndeavourOS_Titan-Nova-2026.08.15.iso.sig">signature</a>, <a href="https://mirror.alpix.eu/endeavouros/iso/EndeavourOS_Titan-Nova-2026.08.15.iso.torrent">torrent</a>, <a href="table.php?distribution=endeavour&amp;pkglist=true&amp;version=2026.08.15#pkglist">pkglist</a>).</td>
